{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting","id":1526355,"title":"Has anyone tried to run VTM in a steampunk setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-05T06:39:55-08:00","id":1526355,"title":"Has anyone tried to run VTM in a steampunk setting?","content":"I'm considering running vampire in a steampunk setting. I literally just thought of it minutes ago, so I don't have any ideas on the campaign beyond that. Can you guys give me any suggestions on running such a game? Literally any ideas would be welcome: plot hooks, how vampires would have easier/harder times with the masquerade in such a setting, how the clans would be different in such a setting, anything that pops into your head about vampire in a steampunk setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T07:37:58-08:00","id":1526356,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: the Wyld West had a crossover event with Deadlands, way back in the day. It might be worth looking at to mine for ideas.<br /> <br /> Eh? Eh? Get it? Because of ghost rock from Deadlands. Ah, well, I'll see myself out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T07:50:40-08:00","id":1526357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526356#post1526356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf: the Wyld West had a crossover event with Deadlands, way back in the day. It might be worth looking at to mine for ideas.<br /> <br /> Eh? Eh? Get it? Because of ghost rock from Deadlands. Ah, well, I'll see myself out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but I've never played Deadlands, so whatever joke you just made is just wooshing over my head.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T08:44:30-08:00","id":1526362,"title":"","content":"I haven't, but I can recommend Gurps Steampunk and/or Gurps Weird War II. Gurps Steampunk is pretty straightforward, Gurps Weird War II is a scenario where WWII was fought between mages and monsters and demons and abominations and... Whatever else you'd like, so it's a pretty good source for adding fantasy elements to an otherwise &quot;normal&quot; scenarios.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Monsters Hunters&quot; series also from Gurps is another good source, switching the roles from WoD (it's basically &quot;Hunters Hunted&quot; heavily expanded and with way more details and without putting normal humans as just mere helpless fragile creatures)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T09:31:40-08:00","id":1526363,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, did someone just say that humans weren't fragile in GURPS? GURPS, the simulation over all else system that can send your character to the hospital if they take only a single point of damage, and where anything even close to a heavy hit involves multiple HT rolls to stay conscious and avoid bleeding out?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526357#post1526357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but I've never played Deadlands, so whatever joke you just made is just wooshing over my head.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly still worth looking into. It's a &quot;weird west&quot; setting where the aforementioned material was used to make much higher performance steam machines, to the point of having super science inventions and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T10:44:51-08:00","id":1526364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting#post1526355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm considering running vampire in a steampunk setting. I literally just thought of it minutes ago, so I don't have any ideas on the campaign beyond that. Can you guys give me any suggestions on running such a game? Literally any ideas would be welcome: plot hooks, how vampires would have easier/harder times with the masquerade in such a setting, how the clans would be different in such a setting, anything that pops into your head about vampire in a steampunk setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What excites or interests you about the idea? Steampunk is really broad, it's hard to give any ideas with something more specific. It's kinda like saying &quot;I want to run Vampire in a fantasy setting,&quot; to give anything constructive you need to give a lot more detail about the kind of setting.<br /> <br /> It could be anything from, &quot;Basically Victorian Age Vampire, but with cooler toys&quot; to &quot;The skies are dark from factories belching smoke so vampires stalk the polluted streets of major cities during the day, and encourage more industrialization and the crushing of workers so they can better feed&quot; to &quot;Vampires are hunted by members of the Society for Opposition to Monsters, who have a charter from the Queen, and use a vast steam powered babbage machine to analyze data and find bloodsuckers in their nests and stake guns and wear etheric goggles to block dominate, and vampires are going extinct&quot;<br /> <br /> It really depends on what interests you about steampunk. Do you want alternate history? Do you want the aesthetic? Do you want to explore the social impact of technological advancement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T13:00:06-08:00","id":1526369,"title":"","content":"Like I said in the first post, I'm in the earliest of earliest of earliest levels of brainstorming, and at this point have no concept beyond, &quot;steampunk vampire might be cool&quot;, so I'm open to any ideas of any nature whatsoever involving steampunk.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T14:39:38-08:00","id":1526371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526363#post1526363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, did someone just say that humans weren't fragile in GURPS? GURPS, the simulation over all else system that can send your character to the hospital if they take only a single point of damage, and where anything even close to a heavy hit involves multiple HT rolls to stay conscious and avoid bleeding out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that depends upon how gritty and realistic you want those life and death situations to be. For personal horror like Monsters Hunters, absolutely, make your feeble mortal coil be as fragile as the rules get.<br /> <br /> What I meant is that in Gurps the puny humans do actually have a fighting chance instead of just being toys for the monsters, there's somewhat of an equal footing, even thou the vampires and werewolves and demons and aliens and whatever are still deadly beats to whom you should approach with the uttermost care and cleverness and still rely on lady luck, it is still possible to put them down... AKA, a &quot;Hunters Hunted&quot; game is indeed feasible.<br /> <br /> <br /> But one of the reasons why I cited the Monsters Hunters series is to give a look upon the arsenal that hunters use for the job. Other good source would be Gurps High Tech, and maybe even Ultra Tech and Bio Tech, although those are more futuristic and not exactly Steampunk, but it could be adapted.<br /> <br /> I also have a few small supplements that are great, just let me find... One is &quot;Weird Science&quot; and &quot;Powers: Weird&quot; (that last one may not be applicable to WoD), but I also had one about fantastic past technology &quot;Gadgets&quot;, like for example &quot;Arquimedes Mirrors&quot; that are used for some kind of &quot;laser beam&quot; weapons, and similar fantastic &quot;old tech&quot; creations (that are pure &quot;retro tech&quot; fantasy).<br /> <br /> A good source of inspiration would be the animation &quot;Steamboy&quot;, this is an awesome movie and shows really fantastic steampunk tech (and is one of the inspirations for my Sons of Ether mages)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T14:46:02-08:00","id":1526374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526364#post1526364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What excites or interests you about the idea? Steampunk is really broad, it's hard to give any ideas with something more specific. It's kinda like saying &quot;I want to run Vampire in a fantasy setting,&quot; to give anything constructive you need to give a lot more detail about the kind of setting.<br /> <br /> It could be anything from, &quot;Basically Victorian Age Vampire, but with cooler toys&quot; to &quot;The skies are dark from factories belching smoke so vampires stalk the polluted streets of major cities during the day, and encourage more industrialization and the crushing of workers so they can better feed&quot; to &quot;Vampires are hunted by members of the Society for Opposition to Monsters, who have a charter from the Queen, and use a vast steam powered babbage machine to analyze data and find bloodsuckers in their nests and stake guns and wear etheric goggles to block dominate, and vampires are going extinct&quot;<br /> <br /> It really depends on what interests you about steampunk. Do you want alternate history? Do you want the aesthetic? Do you want to explore the social impact of technological advancement?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with &quot;Steampunk&quot; genre is that this is basically purely an aesthetic genre. It is almost always assumed a &quot;Victorian Age&quot; style of society simply because. But there has never really being made an effort towards doing a &quot;sociological study&quot; (ficticious) on how such technological developments would actually affect society at large. Would be have somewhat what we have today but with huge machines everywhere? How would the militaries structures change with, I don't know, soldiers wearing clunky, noisy but powerful steam exoskeletons? How would everyday life change?<br /> <br /> Steampunk for that reason is largely used as an aesthetic scenario, with Victorian Era society simply because that's the &quot;point of divergence&quot;, so that you can focus on the &quot;cool stuff&quot; without having to worry about what kinds of steam machines regular people would use in their households to cut their potatoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T14:52:45-08:00","id":1526375,"title":"","content":"I just found 2 interesting supplements you might wanna like, that are way more to the point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/steamtech/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.sjgames.com/navbar/eiphome.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/steamtech/\" target=\"_blank\"> GURPS Steam-Tech </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/steamtech/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/steamtech/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This first is Gurps Steam Techs, describing a ton of interesting fantastic steampunk techs, from vehicles to guns and more<br /> <br /> And now, something that may be more to your liking:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/screampunk/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.sjgames.com/navbar/eiphome.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/screampunk/\" target=\"_blank\"> GURPS Screampunk </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/screampunk/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/screampunk/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is &quot;Gurps Screampunk&quot;, it mixes the genre of the aesthetics of Steampunk with the genre of Horror... So, this may be a bit more in tone to &quot;Steampunk vampires&quot;.<br /> <br /> And this one is just $4, so it's also a cheap choice<br /> <br /> Edit: wow, I just bought it, and it is way better than I initially thought. This is a very short book, only 37 pages long, but it will give you a vast array of material to work with. It has a heavy Faustian tone to it, with a bit of &quot;Dr Frankstein&quot; in it, with the best of Victorian&quot;gothic horror. I'll leave you with a quote from the beginning:<br /> <br /> &quot;If gothic horror reflects the fears of the past, gothic steampunk reflects the Victorian fears of the future&quot;<br /> <br /> Expect a lot of &quot;things-men-were-not-meant-to-know&quot; or &quot;playing as God&quot; or in other words, &quot;overturning the natural order&quot; in it, I think you'll like it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-05-2023, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T23:41:20-08:00","id":1526389,"title":"","content":"I will second the recommendations for GURPS Steampunk and Screampunk. You may also get some mileage out of Cthulhu by Gaslight. And, obviously, Victorian Age Vampire.<br /> <br /> There is a massive amount of Victorian historical fiction, especially detective novels, that deal with the seedier side of society (Anne Perry is a favorite of mine), as well as steampunk fiction that is kind of hit or miss in quality. But that much reading may be overkill. <br /> <br /> You might want to find a summary of William Gibson &amp; Bruce Stirling's The Difference Engine to mine for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T01:18:20-08:00","id":1526392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526374#post1526374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steampunk for that reason is largely used as an aesthetic scenario</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and you don't even need the Victorian Age as an origin point. If you ever played some of the Thief games (first two in particular), you know Dark Age + Steampunk + Supernatural could actually work quite well as an aesthetic framework for a Vampire game. I've always liked that spin on it because you don't see it as often.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T20:58:05-08:00","id":1526494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526392#post1526392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, and you don't even need the Victorian Age as an origin point. If you ever played some of the Thief games (first two in particular), you know Dark Age + Steampunk + Supernatural could actually work quite well as an aesthetic framework for a Vampire game. I've always liked that spin on it because you don't see it as often.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually makes me think of something from the Castlevania Netflix series: the notion that vampires frequently managed to hold onto, and build upon, science and technology that were discovered in ancient times, but then lost during times of turbulence. If you wanted a Steampunk setting where the Steampunk stuff comes earlier in history, vampires could be the source of that technology in your setting; they could still be manipulating things from the shadows through puppets, or maybe lord openly over Steampunk fiefdoms with armies of ghouls in steam-powered tanks, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T22:57:08-08:00","id":1526498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526494#post1526494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you wanted a Steampunk setting where the Steampunk stuff comes earlier in history, vampires could be the source of that technology in your setting; they could still be manipulating things from the shadows through puppets, or maybe lord openly over Steampunk fiefdoms with armies of ghouls in steam-powered tanks, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is... this is almost happened<br /> Heron of Alexandria was a Greek-Egyptian mathematician and inventor.<br /> He made and described in detail what is thought to be the first working steam engine. He called it an aeolipile, or &quot;wind ball&quot;. <br /> It is unknown if Heron's aeolipile ever was put to any practical use in ancient times, but commonly belived it never really caught up because the existeance of slaves - who needs steam engine when slaves do the work for you? Simply it was not needed<br /> But this is one of those things that easly could have gone in a very different way, kicking up the industrial revolution almost 2000 years early<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T23:31:48-08:00","id":1526500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526371#post1526371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that depends upon how gritty and realistic you want those life and death situations to be. For personal horror like Monsters Hunters, absolutely, make your feeble mortal coil be as fragile as the rules get.<br /> <br /> What I meant is that in Gurps the puny humans do actually have a fighting chance instead of just being toys for the monsters, there's somewhat of an equal footing, even thou the vampires and werewolves and demons and aliens and whatever are still deadly beats to whom you should approach with the uttermost care and cleverness and still rely on lady luck, it is still possible to put them down... AKA, a &quot;Hunters Hunted&quot; game is indeed feasible.<br /> <br /> <br /> But one of the reasons why I cited the Monsters Hunters series is to give a look upon the arsenal that hunters use for the job. Other good source would be Gurps High Tech, and maybe even Ultra Tech and Bio Tech, although those are more futuristic and not exactly Steampunk, but it could be adapted.<br /> <br /> I also have a few small supplements that are great, just let me find... One is &quot;Weird Science&quot; and &quot;Powers: Weird&quot; (that last one may not be applicable to WoD), but I also had one about fantastic past technology &quot;Gadgets&quot;, like for example &quot;Arquimedes Mirrors&quot; that are used for some kind of &quot;laser beam&quot; weapons, and similar fantastic &quot;old tech&quot; creations (that are pure &quot;retro tech&quot; fantasy).<br /> <br /> A good source of inspiration would be the animation &quot;Steamboy&quot;, this is an awesome movie and shows really fantastic steampunk tech (and is one of the inspirations for my Sons of Ether mages)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Still doubtful. Multi-hundred point differences in characteristics that adjust raw power tend to leave something a bit smaller than a fighting chance. It's always been about diversions and distractions, because the moment the monster concentrates on you, you're dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T15:30:50-08:00","id":1526530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526500#post1526500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still doubtful. Multi-hundred point differences in characteristics that adjust raw power tend to leave something a bit smaller than a fighting chance. It's always been about diversions and distractions, because the moment the monster concentrates on you, you're dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah of course, if there's hundreds of points of difference between the puny humans and the &quot;things-men-were-not-meant-to-know&quot;, then your hunt is an entirely different kind. The Monster Hunters characters are built with 400 points thou, so those are pretty resourceful humans, pretty skilled and smart and badass veterans, not just comon Joes. But hey, in the series you can even have wrathful ANGELS as antagonists, so yeah, despite those hunters being badasses, sometimes they are indeed dealing with unparalleled supernatural foes. That's part of the fun, to prevail against all odds, using the best of your skills and bravery and any available resources at hand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-08-2023, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T15:43:30-08:00","id":1526531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526498#post1526498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is... this is almost happened<br /> Heron of Alexandria was a Greek-Egyptian mathematician and inventor.<br /> He made and described in detail what is thought to be the first working steam engine. He called it an aeolipile, or &quot;wind ball&quot;.<br /> It is unknown if Heron's aeolipile ever was put to any practical use in ancient times, but commonly belived it never really caught up because the existeance of slaves - who needs steam engine when slaves do the work for you? Simply it was not needed<br /> But this is one of those things that easly could have gone in a very different way, kicking up the industrial revolution almost 2000 years early<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, this would be a very interesting and fun twist! Let's imagine &quot;Roma Aeterna: Steampunk&quot;. Or &quot;Steampunk Athens&quot;. It would make for a very rich environment to have steampunk exoskeleton Greek phalanx fighting against Persian steam tanks... This could work pretty well.<br /> <br /> I saw a crazy TV series once that featured a Leonardo Da Vinci building crazy steam tanks, then some sort of weird guru who was guiding him stole those inventions (from his mind - yeah, the guru mind read Da Vinci's inventions) and gave them to the Ottomans, and that Guru was part of some weird conspiracy that was against both Islam and Christianity... It was some insane TV series, I don't even remember the name of it. But it had &quot;Mage the Ascension&quot; vibes written all over it, and it was late medieval steampunk-ish... It was crazy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it could be fun and perhaps a breath of fresh air to settle the steampunk background on another period other than just Victorian Era. Ancient Greece/Rome Steampunk or Medieval Steampunk both could work very well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T15:59:05-08:00","id":1526533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526530#post1526530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah of course, if there's hundreds of points of difference between the puny humans and the &quot;things-men-were-not-meant-to-know&quot;, then your hunt is an entirely different kind. The Monster Hunters characters are built with 400 points thou, so those are pretty resourceful humans, pretty skilled and smart and badass veterans, not just comon Joes. But hey, in the series you can even have wrathful ANGELS as antagonists, so yeah, despite those hunters being badasses, sometimes they are indeed dealing with unparalleled supernatural foes. That's part of the fun, to prevail against all odds, using the best of your skills and bravery and any available resources at hand</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're human, the hit locations are merciless. If you can regenerate HT an regrow limbs, it's less of a problem. If you're bound by human limitations, though, major wounds to even a single leg means that you're going to need a transfusion, because about a third of your blood just left you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T12:47:08-08:00","id":1526564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1526355-has-anyone-tried-to-run-vtm-in-a-steampunk-setting?p=1526533#post1526533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're human, the hit locations are merciless. If you can regenerate HT an regrow limbs, it's less of a problem. If you're bound by human limitations, though, major wounds to even a single leg means that you're going to need a transfusion, because about a third of your blood just left you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The monsters will always be... Monstrous. But what I meant is that you'll have a fighting chance. Of course, nothing like being ambushed by a dozen vampires and kung-fu them all, that's not what I meant. If you lay in your bed and the vamp was waiting in the closet, you're obviously dead. But a well trained and motivated group of hunters can put down many beasts. Never an easy or safe job of course, but it's doable. In WoD thou, even the lowest neonates are like epic bosses for regular humans thou","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}